[b]Welcome, lords and ladies of KINGDOMS![/b]
It's Friday and bugs fixes are coming! Before you'll jump to the full list of changes/fixes here are some most important ones that I would like to point: 
1) Small, but very useful addition - now quest can be deleted manually from the journal. I know, that many of you asked about this feature, so here we are.
2) Some tweaks in archery - I've changed physical mass of most arrows and this increased their speed and trajectory calculation - this should improve hunting with a bow a bit.
And as usual - thanks a LOT for all your reports (F11 in-game) - this really helps Kingdoms to move a bit closer to the game we all want to play! So, thank you!
The rest of fixes/changes follow:

[b]CHANGES[/b]
[list]
[*]Now player can delete quest right from the journal;
[*]To delete a quest player has to press delete button twice;
[*]Now player has to confirm deletion of a save by pressing delete button twice;
[*]Now arriving settlers with high trader perks will have higher amount of gold (500, 1000, 2000, 5000) - this should boost early-game economy a bit;
[*]Now successful talking or gifting will increase friendship with settler as well;
[*]Arrows physics mass parameters were tweaked a bit in order to improve hunting with a bow;
[/list]
[b]FIXES[/b]
[list]
[*]Fixed bugged collider in big tavern;
[*]Now player can't take quest to destroy his own bandit's lair (already bugged quest can be deleted manually);
[*]Fixed issue when quest icon position could stuck at place for some moment;
[*]Fixed issue when marked settlement icon could lead to incorrect position sometimes;
[*]Fixed issue when quest name could be read if it was too long - because of incorrect font size;
[*]Fixed bugged death animations if settler was killed when working in a war-camp;
[*]Fixed font sizes in game-mode and nobility-choice UI descriptions;
[*]Fixed issue when quest-building-perks panel could gone missing sometimes;
[*]Fixed issue when player's hands could loop in bow shooting animation;
[/list]
[b]LOCALIZATIONS[/b]
[list]
[*]Russian translation was updated;
[*]Brazilian Portuguese translation was updated (big thanks to Kyo!);
[*]Fixed some grammar errors in English text;
[/list]
